<title>USA: Lowe's sees Q4 EPS &quot;around&quot; $0.29.</title>
<headline>Lowe's sees Q4 EPS &quot;around&quot; $0.29.</headline>
<dateline>NORTH WILKESBORO, N.C. 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lowe's Cos Inc said Thursday it was &quot;comfortable&quot; with Wall Street's consensus fourth quarter earnings estimate of &quot;around&quot; $0.29 a share.</p>
<p>In last year's fourth quarter, ended January 31, the company reported diluted earnings per share of $0.23 a share on sales of $1.7 billion.</p>
<p>The company, which reported December same-store sales rose 4.0 percent from a year earlier, said sales were hurt by its move in mid-1996 to limit its consumer electronics assortment, but the move improved gross margins.  </p>
<p>Lowe's said January's weather and year-end inventory adjustments remain variables that could affect its final results.</p>
</text>
